From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] services: a service whose process ends is stopped, whatever state it was in

services.exe's process monitor stopped a service whose process ended only when
the service was RUNNING. A service whose process ended while it was starting
(it had reported START_PENDING), stopping or paused kept that state for ever
with no process: "sc query" said START_PENDING, StartService said the service
was already running, and installers that wait for the service waited for ever.
WireGuard for Windows' installer hung at "install manager service" this way
(its manager service ended on a missing sechost export right after reporting
START_PENDING; i0977). As on Windows, the service is now stopped whatever state
it was in, with ERROR_PROCESS_ABORTED (1067, "The process terminated
unexpectedly"), and its failure actions run -- except when it ended while it
was asked to stop, which is no failure.

Test: test/svcsubscribe-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit): a service that reports
START_PENDING and ends is stopped with 1067 and starts again. Mutant
SG_MUTANT_EXIT_RUNNING_ONLY (programs/services/services.c) fails it.
---
--- a/programs/services/services.c
+++ b/programs/services/services.c
@@ -2076,8 +2076,19 @@
         scmdatabase_lock(db);
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(service, &db->services, struct service_entry, entry)
         {
+            BOOL stopping;
+
+            /* any state but stopped: a service whose process ends while it is starting (it reported
+             * START_PENDING, or never connected) or paused is stopped as well, as Windows does --
+             * it stayed "starting" with no process, and StartService and installers that wait for it
+             * waited for ever (WireGuard's manager service, i0977) */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_EXIT_RUNNING_ONLY
             if (service->status.dwCurrentState != SERVICE_RUNNING || !service->process
+#else
+            if (service->status.dwCurrentState == SERVICE_STOPPED || !service->process
+#endif
                     || service->process->process_id != pid) continue;
+            stopping = service->status.dwCurrentState == SERVICE_STOP_PENDING;
 
             WINE_TRACE("Stopping service %s.\n", debugstr_w(service->config.lpBinaryPathName));
             service->status.dwCurrentState = SERVICE_STOPPED;
@@ -2093,7 +2104,8 @@
             process->use_count--;
             release_process(process);
             notify_service_state(service);
-            service_failed(service, TRUE);
+            /* ending while it was asked to stop is no failure */
+            if (!stopping) service_failed(service, TRUE);
         }
         scmdatabase_unlock(db);
     }
